Fancy on the WebKitGTK 4 API, the compose header built before its signals
fire, and the file chooser treated as the native dialog it is.

1. The Fancy HTML viewer still connected two signals of the old WebKit API
   ("resource-request-starting", "resource-load-failed") that a
   WebKitWebView no longer has -- GObject criticals on every message.  Remote
   content is already filtered by the web extension's send-request handler
   and cid: parts are served by the "cid" URI scheme, so the request handler
   goes; load errors are now taken from each resource's "failed" signal.

2. Its context-menu handler walked WebKit's menu with gtk_container_foreach()
   and appended a GtkMenuItem to it, but the menu is a WebKitContextMenu, not
   a GtkMenu: a critical on every right-click, and none of it ever worked.
   The viewer's entries are now WebKitContextMenuItems made from GActions:
   links open in the browser and download with the viewer's own download,
   "Open Link" in the view only while remote content may be loaded, and
   RSSyl's "Import feed".  The link is copied, since the hit-test result it
   comes from does not outlive the signal.  The never-implemented image
   stubs are gone; WebKit's own image entries stay.

3. The web extension set G_MESSAGES_DEBUG for its own log domain at start-up,
   printing its debug messages from every web process; they now show only
   when asked for (G_MESSAGES_DEBUG=Fancy-Web-Ext).

4. Opening a compose window: the From name's "changed" handler was connected
   before the name was filled in, and retitled the window from a subject
   entry and a window that did not exist yet (criticals from
   gtk_editable_get_chars and gtk_window_set_title).  Connected afterwards.

5. filesel.c made a GtkFileChooserNative transient and modal with the
   GtkWindow calls (criticals at every attach/save); it uses the native
   dialog calls now.

